\f1\fs22 The references, lifted directly from The Chronicles of The Dawkins, were unmistakable to the well-read gathering. The vast congestion of tearful Elvi clapped and cheered wildly, jumping and hugging each other at random, but the jubilation was soon replaced with panic. A group of five Elvi were lying flat, frothing at the mouth, in an apparent fit, each with ear-phones attached to a prehistoric music device. A small group gathered around them, one Elvis took the earphones from one of the Elvi, still jerking about on the ground and listened. His eyes widened and then threw the teeny speakers to the ground.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Gospel music!!\'94 He yelled and then vomited, stumbling as best he could for the nearest exit. Screams of panic filled the air as Elvi clamoured over each other in urgency and desperation, all heading in any direction away from the reviled tunes. The High Elvis rushed from the stage and stood before them in horror. They were not fitting, not like any epileptic he had ever seen. They were jerking about and talking some absolute gibberish as white foam spilled over their chins and the front of their jackets, running rivers of drool and bubbles between the rhinestones. Every so often, they would simultaneously break out into shouts of \'93Praise be to Jesus! The Lord and Saviour! Pledge now, pledge now.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Blasphemy! Get these men out of here immediately.\'94 His inauguration reduced to farce, the High Elvis roared with anger . 
\f2\i What the hell has brought this on? 
\f1\i0 \'93Get them to a secure location and find out what they\'92ve been up to.\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Upon hearing the name of the ancient deity, Jesus, the manic Elvi ran away in disgust and fear, tugging at their hair and reefing out handfuls of jet black locks. They too, in their revulsion, called out, \'93Blasphemy\'94, \'93Apostate\'94 and \'93Unbeliever.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>* * *\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What has happened to them?\'94 the High Elvis asked of the Minister for Internal Security. \'93That display has sent a shock wave though our fledgling nation.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93They are suffering from an extreme case of Evangelism and we are all susceptible if exposure is protracted. According to what they have told us, they were researching old texts, ancient songs and music of the black discs when they stumbled across some hymns. It started out innocently enough, but they ended up with a dependency. The harmonies of Gospel are just too powerful for an Elvis to resist, they are all completely infected with Christianity and unresponsive to evidence based thought or rational argument.\'94 The Minister for Internal Security, was completely exhausted from hours of reasoned debate being met with the deliberately obtuse. \'93It started with a small choir, but by the end they were conducting white masses, baptising each other and then got into sexual abstinence.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Celibacy? That\'92s just plain sick. Is there much hope for them?\'94 the High Elvis hoped they would just snap out of it, but this sounded far too serious for a miracle cure. He had only been in the chair for five minutes when this dangerous meme popped up to spoil the show. If it spread his people could turn away from the true path and embrace blind faith. Something unthinkable.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Personally, I am not hopeful, but none of us have any experience in these matters. Until today we were both low-rent entertainers.\'94 The Minister for Internal Security was still getting used to his lofty new position. \'93We have the welfare of the entire Elvi to protect and need some expert advice.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93It is good to see that you are also humbled by the burden of leadership. We must seek the counsel of the Wise Three. Send a delegation to the Travelator to locate Kleo, Solo and Chilo and invite them to walk among our number, spreading The Dawkins\'92 grace. They will know how to treat our diseased brothers.\'94 the High Elvis did not know if they could help, he wanted to project strength and confidence. \'93We will have to do something about this gospel music. Find out if it is an isolated case or if there is a larger infection, Mr Minister for Health..\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What? Yes, of course, High Elvis.\'94 The new minister was still getting used to the title. \'93To ensure no further outbreaks, I would suggest a complete ban on Gospel music or, for that matter, any music with a religious context.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I really don\'92t wish to resort to censorship, there are always too many grey areas, but it may be the only way. What is the alternative? If there is an outbreak of this meme it could infect us all. We have to keep a lid on this and squash it down hard.\'94 His fondest hope was for his beloved Elvi to practice their art in any way they deemed fit. Blocking an avenue of expression, as one of the first acts of his administration, did not augur well.
